DHAForms — Support

Thank you for using DHAForms, a free reference application for forms published by the South African Department of Home Affairs.

DHAForms is an independent application and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the South African Department of Home Affairs.

Getting help

If you have a question, encounter a problem, or would like to request a form, please contact:

888jjm@gmail.com

The developer is based in Johannesburg (UTC+2) and will respond within one business day where possible.

When reporting a problem, it is helpful to include:

the device you are using (iPhone, iPad, or Mac) and its operating system version;

the version and build number of DHAForms, shown at the bottom of the Settings screen;

the name or code of the form involved (for example, DHA-24);

a brief description of what you expected to happen and what happened instead.

Frequently asked questions

Is DHAForms an official Department of Home Affairs application?
No. DHAForms is an independent application produced by a private developer. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the Department of Home Affairs or any other organ of the South African government.

Does DHAForms submit my application to Home Affairs?
No. DHAForms produces a completed PDF that you may then print or share. Submission of any application to the Department remains the responsibility of the user and must be made through the Department's own channels.

How often are new forms added?
New forms are added on an approximately weekly basis. The library is expanded continuously as additional Home Affairs forms are catalogued, and existing forms are updated where the Department publishes a revised version. Application updates appear on the App Store as they are released.

Which forms can be completed inside the app?
The assisted-completion workflow currently supports DHA-9, DHA-24, DHA-73, and DHA-132. Additional forms are added to the workflow in subsequent releases. Every other form in the catalogue is available as a blank PDF that you can download, share, or print from the Forms tab.

Can I request a specific form?
Yes. Please send the form code or title to the support email above and it will be considered for inclusion in the next release.

Is my information shared with anyone?
No. DHAForms has no servers, no analytics, and no advertising. Your information stays on your device and, where you have enabled iCloud, in your own private iCloud account. See the Privacy Policy for full details.

Does the application work without an internet connection?
Yes. All core features — browsing offices, opening blank forms, and completing forms in the wizard — work offline. An internet connection is only required for iCloud synchronisation between your own devices.

How do I move my data to a new device?
Sign into the new device with the same Apple ID, enable iCloud, and install DHAForms. Your data will synchronise automatically.

Accuracy

DHAForms reproduces publicly available Home Affairs forms for convenience. Users remain responsible for confirming current requirements, form versions, and submission procedures with the Department of Home Affairs before lodging any application. DHAForms does not provide legal advice and makes no representation regarding the outcome of any application submitted to the Department.
